WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.450
- [Narrator] Across the country more than

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.480
half a million people rely on a service dog

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.693
in their everyday life.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.460
These elite dogs are the product of

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.563
months of schooling.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.280
And not all puppies that begin training

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.483
have what it takes to become a service dog.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.280
If a pup doesn't live up to the strict

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.573
standards required they will fail out.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.810
Which puppies have the brains and behavior

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.600
to make it through the rigors of training?

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.433
We find out

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:21.673
at Puppy Prep.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.700
(light music)

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.660
On the California coastline,

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.260
about half way between Los Angeles

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.023
and San Francisco sits Arroyo Grande.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.970
A small community of beaches,

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.313
mountains and wineries.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.133
Just outside of town is Doggie Do Good.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.010
A training and obedience school specializing

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.773
in the education of service dogs.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.023
Depending on the dog,

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.980
the journey from carefree puppy to hero

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.660
can take anywhere from six months

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.873
to more than a year.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.760
Not all dogs make it through the process.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.893
If a dog flunks out,

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.210
it's put up for adoption.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.490
At any given time,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.280
there are dozens of service dogs in

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.580
training at Doggy Do Good.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.460
The abilities they learn range from

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:40.803
retrieval, to stability, pressure therapy,

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.143
medical alerts, simply kisses,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.593
and much more.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.240
What they learn depends upon what each

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.343
individual dog is predisposed to.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.003
For instance,

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:57.190
^yellow lab, Deacon, specializes in

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.623
^retrieval and stability.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.423
- Good, steady.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.090
- [Narrator] At almost two years old,

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.700
he's older than many of the dogs that

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.270
have already graduated.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.493
He was a stubborn pup.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:07.810
And though he had come close to

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.643
flunking out,

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.810
he is now only weeks from

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.083
potential graduation.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.283
Still, he can't coast.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.330
Until the minute before graduating,

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.420
trainers are watching the dogs for any sign

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.120
that they won't be able to cut it.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:23.793
Right now,

00:02:23.793 --> 00:02:25.060
Deacon and his classmate are working

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.373
on basic come drills.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.590
The pups run around the lawn and play.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.840
And one by one the trainers call out to them.

00:02:30.892 --> 00:02:31.725
- Kaya, come.

00:02:31.725 --> 00:02:32.558
Good girl.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:34.643
- Cooper, come.

00:02:36.673 --> 00:02:37.506
Good boy.

00:02:37.506 --> 00:02:38.339
- [Narrator] The most important thing a

00:02:38.339 --> 00:02:39.210
dog needs to learn is the difference

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.143
between playtime and work time.

00:02:41.781 --> 00:02:43.400
While it's alright for the dogs

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.400
to act like puppies,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.210
as soon as the trainers calls them

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.860
they need to snap into work mode.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.913
These drills help solidify that skill.

00:02:53.121 --> 00:02:53.954
- [Trainer] Deacon, come.

00:02:53.954 --> 00:02:55.150
- [Narrator] For a veteran like Deacon,

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:55.983
this is simple.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.763
If Deacon is a senior in service dog high,

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.680
one of the incoming freshman

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:04.513
^is Kaya.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.450
^An eight month old golden retriever.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.313
Kaya is beautiful and I love her.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.400
If she fails out of school during training,

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.900
I will be trying to adopt her.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.963
And right off the bat she's having a problem.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.900
See, Kaya enjoys the company of people

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.003
over other dogs.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.130
While it's good to be comfortable around people,

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:29.230
she can't remain nervous around other dogs

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.830
if she's going to pass training.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.090
^Kaya's half sister, Remmy,

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.523
^is also starting class.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.590
Though they share a dad and are almost

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.610
the same age Remmy has a

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:47.260
completely different personality.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.580
Remmy loves to play with other dogs.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.160
And often tries to pull her half sister

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.363
out of her doggie shell.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.623
^For the especially young pups,

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.740
^like six month old chocolate lab, Beneli,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.190
learning the come command begins on a long leash.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.543
A trainer call Beneli and gives a gentle tug.

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.360
This one little pull is all the puppy needs

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.760
to come the rest of the way.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.480
Until she recognizes the command,

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:16.010
the leash helps Beneli understand

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.490
what the English speaking humans

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.690
are trying to communicate to her doggy ears.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.389
So far she's doing an,

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:23.222
Cleo!

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.270
Stop getting everyone into trouble.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.460
Keep it it up, Beneli,

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:31.480
and you'll be off that leash in no time.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.853
After this morning exercise,

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.970
it's time to try something more subdued.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.110
Most of the service dog's time isn't spent

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.993
running around or actively working.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.500
Instead being calm and on call.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.263
Ready at a moment's notice to help.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.450
The puppies must lay down and not get

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.350
distracted for long stretches of time.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.960
Trainers toss toys around to make sure the

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.813
dogs will choose their jobs over pure playtime.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.943
- [Trainer] Good stay, guys.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.240
- [Narrator] Whenever a dog breaks from their

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.270
down stay it isn't enough for the dog to

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.533
simply lay back down.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:12.990
The trainer needs to take the dog

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.840
back to the position where they were.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.370
Otherwise a puppy won't understand the

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.470
gravity of getting up.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.170
If a dog is always distracted,

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.523
and can't learn to focus,

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.750
that's the quickest way to fail Puppy Prep.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.343
Kaya's brother, Luke, is late to class.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.350
He spent the morning offsite with a trainer.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.510
And without having the morning to run around,

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.020
like the rest of his classmates,

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.770
Luke may be too bored to sit still.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.680
Beneli, all you have to do is

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.033
literally stay still.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.040
If Beneli can't stay when the ball is

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.010
tossed over her head,

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.420
she may become too distracted when

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.423
taken out in public.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.143
Remmy!

00:05:56.143 --> 00:05:57.003
Come on,

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.033
you pups just need to relax.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.720
These two have just started,

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.993
so their behavior isn't a huge problem yet.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:08.200
Kaya, however is just as new and already

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.343
a pro at down stay.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.770
That's why you're my favorite.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.390
With most of the dogs being unfazed

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.223
by the toys,

00:06:15.223 --> 00:06:17.270
it's time for some livelier distractions.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:21.873
Oh my God,

00:06:21.873 --> 00:06:22.706
^it's Mr. Pip!

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.910
^Mr. Pip is beyond

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.453
being absolutely undeniable,

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.180
also a service dog in training.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.160
Smaller dogs can comfort people with anxiety,

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.910
as well as help alert people with diseases

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.260
like diabetes when they need to

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.260
take their medicine.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.430
Now, however, his only job

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.930
is to distract his classmates.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.112
Most of the dogs don't fall for the enchanting

00:06:42.112 --> 00:06:43.633
dance of Mr. Pip.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.913
^Except for Tank, the german shepherd.

00:06:47.712 --> 00:06:49.100
^One thing that Tank

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.883
needs to work on is his play drive.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.850
Small animals like cats and Mr. Pip

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.670
can distract larger dogs when they're with

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:57.713
their future owners.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.250
Tank must fight his most basic instincts

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.650
in order to pass Puppy Prep.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.040
And as for Mr. Pip,

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.233
he isn't scared.

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:07.893
He has a job to do but he performs it admirably.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.473
God bless you, Mr. Pip.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.500
By the end of the down stay lesson,

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.483
it looks like everyone's made progress.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.763
But there's one more test.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.243
^Mercy.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.433
A malinois with almost unlimited energy.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:30.880
Mercy belongs to Sandy,

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.313
the owner of Doggy Do Good.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:38.973
Immaculately schooled.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.343
Mercy acts as a four legged trainer.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.640
Squeaking the toy just as the

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:43.740
people trainers would.

00:07:45.029 --> 00:07:47.196
(barking)

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.963
Mercy's claimed a victim.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.903
With only a month from his planned graduation,

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.390
Deacon should know better than to

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.440
break from down stay.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.633
If he continues to lose focus,

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.110
he may have to stay in school for extra months.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.463
Or worse, flunk out.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:04.910
As for the other dogs

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.680
they've taken their lessons well.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.610
For most it's still early in their

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:09.723
service dog training.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.180
As long as they can keep making progress

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:14.440
the puppies show good promise of graduating.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.610
Kaya in particular,

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.093
shows a lot of potential.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.890
Especially for her young age and upbringing.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.510
Unlike her brother, Luke,

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:24.070
who was raised since birth by trainers

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.083
at Doggy Do Good,

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.403
Kaya went off to a puppy raiser family.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:29.300
Many of the dogs at Doggy Do Good

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.670
live with a foster family for the

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.220
first few months of their life.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.490
There, they learn the most basic behaviors.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.490
Like potty training.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.640
When pups reach six to eight months

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.370
they return to Doggy Do Good to begin

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.453
service dog school.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.260
Kaya's family dropped her off a few

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:44.560
weeks ago and she's seen them only once since.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.313
Today, however, they're back for a visit.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.010
When trainer, Paul, brings Kaya outside,

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.710
she thinks she's going for a walk.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.650
What she doesn't know is that the family

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.900
that raised her is waiting around the corner.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:57.883
- [Dad] Kaya.

00:08:57.961 --> 00:08:59.044
- [Sis] Kaya!

00:08:59.197 --> 00:09:00.030
Hi Kaya!

00:09:00.957 --> 00:09:01.874
Hi, oh, hi!

00:09:02.738 --> 00:09:07.153
- [Dad] Hey, baby, hey baby.

00:09:07.153 --> 00:09:08.653
- [Mom] Come here.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.513
- [Sis] I miss you.

00:09:09.513 --> 00:09:10.346
- [Narrator] During their training

00:09:10.346 --> 00:09:12.010
it's easy to forget how young the dogs are.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.240
When allowed to roll around with

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.293
her former family,

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.013
Kaya is all puppy.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.890
Even if foster father, Ray, wants to make sure

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:20.963
she still behaves.

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:23.740
Puppy raisers are a crucial part of

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.053
the service dog process.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.043
And often,

00:09:26.043 --> 00:09:28.180
one of the bottlenecks to training service dogs.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:31.060
Newborn puppies need your constant attention

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.710
to learn the basics of obedience.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:35.613
- Good girl.

00:09:35.613 --> 00:09:36.850
- [Narrator] And while it's fun for the family

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:37.793
to raise a puppy,

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.330
knowing they have to say good bye

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.543
in a few short months can be difficult.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.150
Kaya's family is proud of the job

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.163
she'll someday have,

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.740
and while they still miss Kaya,

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.223
the family thinks that soon,

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.910
they'll be ready to take another puppy

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:51.190
to help begin its journey to

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.973
becoming a service dog.

00:09:53.432 --> 00:09:55.920
- Release, release, good girl.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:58.780
- [Narrator] At the end of the day,

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.000
the good boys and good girls at Doggy Do Good

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.980
have taken another step to becoming fully

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:04.183
trained service dogs.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.010
But tomorrow is another day

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.220
filled with new challenges and distractions

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:10.823
that could ruin a dog's career.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:14.173
Which puppies have what it takes?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:16.953
Mr. Pip!

00:10:17.091 --> 00:10:19.318
(laughing)

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:21.818
(light music)

